bin/
# Anchored to the repo root ON PURPOSE. An unanchored `manager` matches any
# path component with that name, which silently swallowed config/manager/ -
# the operator's own deployment manifest - so `git add -A` skipped it for the
# whole of v0.2.0 and the release shipped with no way to deploy the operator.
/manager
*.test
cover.out
.DS_Store

# Every runner directory is `package main`, so `go build ./runners/<name>/` — and
# `go build ./...` — drops an executable called <name> HERE, at the repository
# root, not beside its source. Untracked and unignored, the next `git add -A`
# commits it: that is how a 4.2 MB `ib-write-bw` and a 3.4 MB `host-health` got
# into a public repository.
#
# Anchored for the same reason `/manager` is, and it matters more here: an
# unanchored `nccl` would match runners/nccl/ and make the runner's own source
# invisible to git. runners/pins_test.go derives this list from the filesystem
# and fails if a runner directory has no entry, so a new runner cannot land
# without one.
/clockprobe
/compute-smoke
/dcgm-diag
/gpu-burn
/gpudirect-rdma
/host-health
/ib-write-bw
/memory-bw
/memory-stress
/nccl
/thermal-soak
